# =============================================================================
# JE SALES-INVOICE / CREDIT-MEMO MATCHING PIPELINE  —  ANNOTATED VERSION
# =============================================================================
# HIGH-LEVEL DATA FLOW (read this first):
#
#   JE_raw (current qtr raw export)  ─┐
#   JE_raw_2_aligned (carry-fwd, optional) ─┤
#                                            ▼
#   PIPELINE 1 (Cell 4): match SI<->CM inside JE_raw only (same fiscal year)
#       consumes : JE_raw
#       produces : P1_ALL_MATCHED, P1_ALL_UNMATCHED  (+ many P1_* audit tables)
#                                            │ (P1_ALL_UNMATCHED feeds P2)
#                                            ▼
#   PIPELINE 2 (Cell 5): match CY-unmatched vs PY carry-forward rows
#       consumes : P1_ALL_UNMATCHED (aligned back to raw schema) + JE_raw_2_aligned
#       produces : P2_ALL_MATCHED, P2_ALL_UNMATCHED  (+ many P2_* audit tables)
#                                            │ (P2_ALL_UNMATCHED feeds P3)
#                                            ▼
#   PIPELINE 3 (Cell 6): loose-PK tolerance match (no amount in key, ±100 tol)
#       consumes : P2_ALL_UNMATCHED
#       produces : P3_ONE_TO_MANY, P3_DATE_SYNC, P3_DATE_UNSYNC, P3_NO_MATCH_FOUND
#                                            │ (all 4 unioned = P3_ALL_UNMATCHED)
#                                            ▼
#   AA COMMENT TAGGING (Cell 7): rule-priority labeling of every unmatched row
#       consumes : P3_ALL_UNMATCHED + raw_for_stats (full JE_raw [+ carry-fwd])
#                  + oto (P3's one-to-one candidate table, for exact-cancel check)
#       produces : P3_ALL_UNMATCHED_COMMENTED  (adds "AA Comment" + "AA Rule" cols)
#                                            ▼
#   FINAL EXPORT (Cell 8): union everything, write one Excel workbook,
#                          then assert total_out == total_raw (no rows lost/dup'd)
#
# KEY IDENTIFIER COLUMNS (easy to confuse — keep these straight):
#   row_id          : unique id per raw JE line, assigned once in ensure_row_id().
#                     Follows a row through the ENTIRE pipeline (P1->P2->P3->AA).
#   primary_key     : matching key used in P1/P2 = Company Desc + Vendor# + ABS(amount).
#                     Rows sharing this key are candidates to net against each other.
#   p3_primary_key  : looser P3-only key = Company Desc + Vendor# (NO amount).
#                     Used because P3 allows a tolerance gap instead of exact netting.
#   pair_id         : assigned to a CONFIRMED sales<->credit match, format "<label>_<n>".
#                     Only exists after resolve_to_original(); not present on raw rows.
# =============================================================================


